 In the served composed candidate, hold build information and reach Back/Reload without a mouse. Retry once, deliver the old response late, and confirm only the replacement becomes ready. Fail/timeout startup, retry with the same physical controller and continue into the existing Find/Review menu. Complete startup while Reload is focused, while Back has newer focus and while the page is backgrounded; inspect the actual focus ring and next action. Return from a cached/ordinary history traversal without accidental actions, then explicitly leave. Repeat Theme/Plain and Large reading settings with portrait/short-landscape layout and real touch/controller separately.
 
 Maintainer prompt: “Make startup escape actions navigable before data is ready using one page-owned router. Preserve physical edge history across explicit Reload, cancel only the replaced read/deadline, and never auto-discover profiles. Retire focused Reload to Find only under current foreground ownership; do not defer focus to a later return. Keep the existing read-only reader's Back/Close guarantees and retain actual failed/held/late-response receipts.”
+
+
+## Deferred Back ownership correction
+
+A ready Recovery view closes its reader before asking the host to leave. That asynchronous completion must still belong to the same view, read generation and foreground interaction. A history departure/return or background completion invalidates the old Back request; it cannot navigate or restore focus later. A fresh current Back still works. The final host navigation also checks that pagehide has not invalidated its own continuation. Reader cancellation/closure still completes before legitimate navigation; no data write or automatic inspection is added.
+
+The separate successor on the same a13 + P05 + P03 composition passes six complete affected files: **81/81 each on Node 20.19.5 and 22.22.2**, with 95 unchanged inputs / 1,144,784 bytes, sequentially at 1024 MiB. Five added cases exercise actual host/view/reader behavior through a modeled readonly IndexedDB transaction whose abort completion is held. They cover legitimate and overlapping Back, persisted departure/return, background closure, terminal ready closure and terminal startup continuation. The preceding P03 runtime fails three of those cases (10 pass / 3 fail across the whole 13-case startup file). This is genuine asynchronous reader ownership coverage with a modeled storage-event boundary, not native IndexedDB/BFCache or physical-controller acceptance. Earlier 68/76 cohorts and their immutable packets remain separate evidence.
+
+Prompt: “Preserve close-before-Back but bind a delayed close callback to its originating Recovery view and generation. A newer history visit or background completion must invalidate its navigation; a fresh current Back must still leave once. Use actual reader work with a delayed readonly transaction abort to prove the boundary, preserve prior failed receipts, and do not change profile permissions or automatic discovery.”
